34a0eea-7a26-48ec-8e89-3471b95a224a" class="r-lpnyrj"><picture data-rid="c2976886-f9ec-42b9-9b3b-99705396a566" class="r-1sqsj7o"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/39afbdbf-870a-4720-a8f6-e9e8bd9d26aa/69ab3d1b-e307-4518-aacc-c323ba17cb8a?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/39afbdbf-870a-4720-a8f6-e9e8bd9d26aa/69ab3d1b-e307-4518-aacc-c323ba17cb8a?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/39afbdbf-870a-4720-a8f6-e9e8bd9d26aa/69ab3d1b-e307-4518-aacc-c323ba17cb8a?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/39afbdbf-870a-4720-a8f6-e9e8bd9d26aa/69ab3d1b-e307-4518-aacc-c323ba17cb8a" class="r-1e7h6br" loading="lazy"/></picture><div data-rid="ad434b81-6bc3-4f41-af89-9232238f132f" class="r-1f7t3hz alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Ten Tips for Teens</p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="cf2303c5-6572-4fff-9f1d-7feb3002db6e" class="r-1gohw97"><div data-rid="e5d88f0e-287f-40c0-a078-f49dea4f621a" class="r-1gtdx55"><div data-rid="567f9e3d-5bec-4e4e-8a74-a14ff81aed42" class="r-4wzl54"><div data-rid="b6c15245-2ab4-4c7b-b564-15f561e3976c" class="r-ihafhh alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2></span></div><div data-rid="93d9265e-15de-445a-a503-e58ff87118aa" class="r-jbgra3 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>The questions every family asks before enrolling — answered directly.</p></span></div></div><div class="r-vulslw" data-rid="1"><div data-rid="b81686c8-7dd3-4ec5-9e3e-1ce03589ce99" class="r-1v004tb"><div data-rid="c76b7758-bb24-4d7c-a176-e1c2c74c1a7b" class="r-1v05kon" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="a9f92cd2-76fb-4a19-b4a5-a802b1a43eb8" class="r-1vucny6" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="29eae0ab-64a5-47b8-83be-5939dc393f64" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R5n32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1cqut0m"><div data-rid="c07e3455-b336-4e2c-b8d6-16a02977099a" class="r-1fdzo9l alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What ages is the Academy designed for?</p></span></div><div data-rid="534dc69f-c1e6-42c3-bcaa-ba4788ba5f74" class="r-1mygijo" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:auto;max-height:100%" class="r-hvi54p" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:R5n32:"><div data-rid="a5c5a77b-c6e9-4767-887b-4dbd700494cc" class="r-1rxjktr"><div data-rid="f6ce5e25-382b-4bc4-9031-99532622a088" class="r-clj7d8 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>The Academy is built for teens ages 12–18. Content uses story-based learning with real-world examples that land with teenagers while teaching serious economic, civic, and historical concepts. Younger kids (ages 5–11) can start with our illustrated book series.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="153c543c-b5bf-47e3-8cf6-93287bb14a0f" class="r-bi6uu8" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="e376af94-da0e-4fa6-8400-f87bf52908a2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R9n32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-ihuw8s"><div data-rid="72af92bb-e2c6-49e0-bb77-c5f53db678b2" class="r-1parl6y alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>How does this work with homeschooling?</p></span></div><div data-rid="17c313e1-e373-4160-bf04-0f55cdb85398" class="r-10op4nk" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:auto;max-height:100%" class="r-fmdcy1" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:R9n32:"><div data-rid="5831061a-010c-45ce-b691-d1258692341a" class="r-1a6fhgj"><div data-rid="753f0698-f709-4abb-8572-d6ade48baa86" class="r-1mzpsof alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>It was built for homeschool families. Many use Academy as their core Economics, Civics, and History curriculum — with lesson plans, quizzes, and summaries included at no extra cost. It also works seamlessly as a targeted supplement alongside any existing curriculum.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="3ae2544b-27c0-449c-9b36-3dc0cc9e23dc" class="r-113gn0z" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="0323982e-b0da-4487-821f-dbe703f84a6a" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rdn32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-3nh3jm"><div data-rid="c2e457f0-7500-45c1-81f5-b034d508fc36" class="r-rindrn alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What if my teen doesn't connect with it?</p></span></div><div data-rid="7ef219d6-ff0a-4fd1-a4e2-3908f9253687" class="r-8due1j" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:auto;max-height:100%" class="r-e3h0a" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Rdn32:"><div data-rid="a4e5f9cc-9a6a-45d6-be05-e01fed29e893" class="r-1v8k87p"><div data-rid="3fe3d06f-5aac-418c-999c-f127b7173895" class="r-1l1yd29 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Start with the free lesson — no card, no risk. Our 93% retention rate comes from making the content genuinely interesting, not from locking anyone in. If your teen doesn't love the first lesson, you haven't lost anything. We're confident they will.</p></span></div></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="e6719ac1-d76f-4bc3-abb8-cf5593f33147" class="r-sv21vx" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="f2aa9fe5-c9ce-42db-be31-694514d1f683" class="r-1xy8fdv" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="ef0c1a29-7161-4be8-a787-e6c30d48ee9e" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:R6n32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-ogdstl"><div data-rid="48a8093e-fa3f-4904-b437-4b5a1e752d18" class="r-zewu3l alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Is this too political or biased?</p></span></div><div data-rid="ce0fb466-38d1-41b6-9e2d-6a4876276885" class="r-jyrsul" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:auto;max-height:100%" class="r-1yet44" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:R6n32:"><div data-rid="90b40039-47c8-47a5-ad04-4e0549396e83" class="r-1mj66fx"><div data-rid="d864a14f-c462-4b17-8e82-728fb101535f" class="r-1bgiyx5 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>The Academy is built on the principle that teens should think for themselves — not be told what to think. We teach the ideas behind both freedom and constraint, and we trust teens to evaluate them. Our goal is intellectual tools, not political outcomes.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="485a27c6-0dac-492f-9fcb-beeb337172bd" class="r-ohv3zx" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="5213b979-2e6a-4178-86ec-9ca3428642e5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Ran32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-sp3tvc"><div data-rid="2da8ff4c-698b-42c5-99cb-6a5d99c1de9b" class="r-16clpvr alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Can my teen in public or private school still benefit?</p></span></div><div data-rid="6a27e009-28b5-4b4c-9725-51856c84704c" class="r-1adsp5l" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:auto;max-height:100%" class="r-1k99e4k" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Ran32:"><div data-rid="19a86971-0c77-4990-80b0-1d61ec415986" class="r-1ntptzl"><div data-rid="7e0046a3-9692-4cf2-8645-3c2d7a199576" class="r-1te0awb alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Absolutely — Academy was designed to fill the specific gaps that traditional school leaves behind. Teens use it after school, on weekends, or over summer. Many parents say it's the education they wish they'd received when they were their teenager's age.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="0fb20810-2970-4f45-a95b-967882bf4f6a" class="r-14ahjjl" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="a9b6cd6f-9917-46b1-89e1-d611a92a1140" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Ren32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-tme8w"><div data-rid="186bfe23-ed51-4bf6-8919-dec2ea991f0e" class="r-11a741k alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What's the difference between Lifetime and Annual?</p></span></div><div data-rid="24e4f388-ec7a-4d7a-b98c-ee89ba0bfa74" class="r-8cgg6x" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" st